{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "The opt-in keys of [verify] and what they resolve to (docs/CONTRACTS.md section 53).",
    "Each case is a policy.toml [verify] block (after `command = \"x\"`) and `resolves`: the fields the",
    "resolved block must carry. `absent` lists fields it must not carry, because a key nobody declared",
    "adds nothing to what runs. Asserted by packages/gnomon-core/src/verify_setup.test.ts.",
    "Since #232: the verdict table (`verdicts`, `contracts`) and `exit_cases`: one run of the check with an exit, read by the loop (`gnomon task`) and by `gnomon check` through the same table. `check_status` is the `verify` entry's status in a `gnomon check` verdict (regressed is a fail there: a judge of someone else's change has no model to hand it to).",
    "Since #234: `protects` (docs/CONTRACTS.md section 53). `detected` is what the token `@detected` names besides the files the command itself runs (`command_files`); `digest_cases` say what counts as a change to a protected file, by file. A turn that changes one cannot come out `passed`: `passed_unverified`. Asserted by packages/gnomon-core/src/verify_protects.test.ts.",
    "Since #235: `task_exit` is the exit `gnomon task --require-verify` (or [verify] exit_on_fail) gives a task whose bucket says 0 (a refusal or apparatus failure keeps its own exit); `flag_exit: null` leaves it 0. Without the flag every row is 0 (#211). `doctor_verify` is `gnomon doctor verify`: its schema, exits, finding kinds, and the cases the probe is tested on. Asserted by packages/gnomon-core/src/verify_exit_detail.test.ts."
  ],
  "setup_network": [
    "none",
    "registry"
  ],
  "setup_audit": {
    "kind": "verify",
    "phase": "setup",
    "network": [
      "none",
      "registry"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "nothing declared",
      "verify": {},
      "resolves": {},
      "absent": [
        "timeout_seconds",
        "setup",
        "setup_network",
        "setup_timeout_seconds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a timeout of the check's own",
      "verify": {
        "timeout_seconds": 900
      },
      "resolves": {
        "timeout_seconds": 900
      },
      "absent": [
        "setup"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a setup, network shut by default",
      "verify": {
        "setup": "uv sync --frozen"
      },
      "resolves": {
        "setup": "uv sync --frozen",
        "setup_network": "none"
      },
      "absent": [
        "timeout_seconds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a setup with the registry open",
      "verify": {
        "setup": "pnpm install --frozen-lockfile",
        "setup_network": "registry",
        "setup_timeout_seconds": 1200
      },
      "resolves": {
        "setup_network": "registry",
        "setup_timeout_seconds": 1200
      },
      "absent": []
    },
    {
      "name": "an unreadable timeout is ignored",
      "verify": {
        "timeout_seconds": -5
      },
      "resolves": {},
      "absent": [
        "timeout_seconds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an unknown setup_network is read as none",
      "verify": {
        "setup": "make deps",
        "setup_network": "anywhere"
      },
      "resolves": {
        "setup_network": "none"
      },
      "absent": []
    }
  ],
  "verdicts": [
    "passed",
    "failed",
    "unrunnable",
    "regressed"
  ],
  "contracts": {
    "septacore": {
      "0": "passed",
      "1": "failed",
      "2": "unrunnable",
      "3": "regressed"
    },
    "pytest": {
      "0": "passed",
      "1": "failed",
      "2": "unrunnable",
      "4": "unrunnable",
      "5": "unrunnable"
    }
  },
  "exit_map_values": [
    "failed",
    "unrunnable",
    "regressed"
  ],
  "exit_cases": [
    {
      "name": "no table: exit 0",
      "verify": {},
      "exit": 0,
      "verdict": "passed",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "pass"
    },
    {
      "name": "no table: exit 1",
      "verify": {},
      "exit": 1,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "no table: exit 5 is a failure as before",
      "verify": {},
      "exit": 5,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "no table: exit 127",
      "verify": {},
      "exit": 127,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "pytest: collection error",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "pytest"
      },
      "exit": 2,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "pytest: usage error",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "pytest"
      },
      "exit": 4,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "pytest: no tests collected",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "pytest"
      },
      "exit": 5,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "pytest: a failing test",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "pytest"
      },
      "exit": 1,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "septacore: could not measure",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "septacore"
      },
      "exit": 2,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "septacore: regressed is recorded, not handed back",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "septacore"
      },
      "exit": 3,
      "verdict": "regressed",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "septacore: regressed handed back on request",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "septacore",
        "regressed_hand_back": true
      },
      "exit": 3,
      "verdict": "regressed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "exit_map: a project script's NOT RUN",
      "verify": {
        "exit_map": {
          "4": "unrunnable"
        }
      },
      "exit": 4,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "exit_map over a preset",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "pytest",
        "exit_map": {
          "5": "failed"
        }
      },
      "exit": 5,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "exit_map cannot make a non-zero exit pass",
      "verify": {
        "exit_map": {
          "3": "passed"
        }
      },
      "exit": 3,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "exit_map cannot touch exit 0",
      "verify": {
        "exit_map": {
          "0": "failed"
        }
      },
      "exit": 0,
      "verdict": "passed",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "pass"
    },
    {
      "name": "an unknown preset is no preset",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "jest"
      },
      "exit": 2,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    }
  ],
  "verdicts_task": [
    "passed",
    "passed_unverified",
    "failed",
    "unrunnable",
    "regressed",
    "declined",
    "skipped"
  ],
  "protects": {
    "token": "@detected",
    "detected": [
      "**/conftest.py",
      "pytest.ini",
      "pyproject.toml",
      "package.json",
      ".septacore.json",
      "**/vitest.config.*",
      "**/jest.config.*",
      "tox.ini",
      "setup.cfg",
      "noxfile.py",
      ".coveragerc"
    ],
    "command_files": [
      {
        "command": "bash scripts/verify.sh",
        "files": [
          "scripts/verify.sh"
        ]
      },
      {
        "command": "./run_tests.sh --fast",
        "files": [
          "run_tests.sh"
        ]
      },
      {
        "command": "pytest -q tests/",
        "files": [
          "tests/"
        ]
      },
      {
        "command": "pnpm test",
        "files": []
      },
      {
        "command": "make test",
        "files": [
          "Makefile",
          "makefile",
          "GNUmakefile"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "digest_cases": [
      {
        "name": "a conftest.py edit",
        "file": "conftest.py",
        "before": "a",
        "after": "b",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "a conftest.py left alone",
        "file": "tests/conftest.py",
        "before": "a",
        "after": "a",
        "changed": false
      },
      {
        "name": "a file created",
        "file": "pytest.ini",
        "before": null,
        "after": "[pytest]\n",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "a file deleted",
        "file": ".septacore.json",
        "before": "{}",
        "after": null,
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json: a script",
        "file": "package.json",
        "before": "{\"scripts\":{\"test\":\"a\"}}",
        "after": "{\"scripts\":{\"test\":\"b\"}}",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json: a dependency is not a change",
        "file": "package.json",
        "before": "{\"scripts\":{\"test\":\"a\"}}",
        "after": "{\"scripts\":{\"test\":\"a\"},\"dependencies\":{\"x\":\"1\"}}",
        "changed": false
      },
      {
        "name": "pyproject.toml: addopts",
        "file": "pyproject.toml",
        "before": "[tool.pytest.ini_options]\naddopts = \"-q\"\n",
        "after": "[tool.pytest.ini_options]\naddopts = \"-k nothing\"\n",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "pyproject.toml: another table is not a change",
        "file": "pyproject.toml",
        "before": "[project]\nname = \"a\"\n[tool.pytest.ini_options]\naddopts = \"-q\"\n",
        "after": "[project]\nname = \"b\"\n[tool.pytest.ini_options]\naddopts = \"-q\"\n",
        "changed": false
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json: the jest key",
        "file": "package.json",
        "before": "{\"jest\":{\"bail\":1}}",
        "after": "{\"jest\":{\"bail\":0,\"testPathIgnorePatterns\":[\"x\"]}}",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "setup.cfg: [tool:pytest]",
        "file": "setup.cfg",
        "before": "[tool:pytest]\naddopts = -q\n",
        "after": "[tool:pytest]\naddopts = -k nothing\n",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "setup.cfg: another section is not a change",
        "file": "setup.cfg",
        "before": "[metadata]\nname = a\n[tool:pytest]\naddopts = -q\n",
        "after": "[metadata]\nname = b\n[tool:pytest]\naddopts = -q\n",
        "changed": false
      },
      {
        "name": "a vitest config",
        "file": "vitest.config.ts",
        "before": "a",
        "after": "b",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "a nested jest config",
        "file": "packages/x/jest.config.js",
        "before": "a",
        "after": "b",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "a Makefile under make",
        "file": "Makefile",
        "before": "a",
        "after": "b",
        "changed": true,
        "command": "make test"
      }
    ]
  },
  "task_exit": [
    {
      "verdict": "passed",
      "flag_exit": null
    },
    {
      "verdict": "failed",
      "flag_exit": 1
    },
    {
      "verdict": "regressed",
      "flag_exit": 1
    },
    {
      "verdict": "passed_unverified",
      "flag_exit": 1
    },
    {
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "flag_exit": 4
    },
    {
      "verdict": "declined",
      "flag_exit": null
    },
    {
      "verdict": "skipped",
      "flag_exit": null
    }
  ],
  "task_record_detail": {
    "keys": [
      "verify_exit",
      "verify_rounds",
      "verify_reason",
      "verify_tail"
    ],
    "present_when": [
      "--require-verify",
      "[verify] exit_on_fail = true",
      "[verify] record_detail = true"
    ]
  },
  "doctor_verify": {
    "schema": "gnomon.doctor_verify/1",
    "exits": {
      "clear": 0,
      "attention": 1,
      "couldNotRun": 10
    },
    "kinds": [
      "not_declared",
      "unrunnable",
      "no_tests",
      "ambiguous_exit",
      "red_baseline",
      "dirty_tree",
      "setup_not_run"
    ],
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "passes",
        "exit_code": 0,
        "verdict": "passed",
        "kinds": []
      },
      {
        "name": "not found",
        "exit_code": 1,
        "verdict": "unrunnable",
        "kinds": [
          "unrunnable"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "pytest's no tests collected",
        "exit_code": 1,
        "verdict": "failed",
        "kinds": [
          "ambiguous_exit"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "a usage error",
        "exit_code": 1,
        "verdict": "failed",
        "kinds": [
          "ambiguous_exit"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "a failing check",
        "exit_code": 1,
        "verdict": "failed",
        "kinds": [
          "red_baseline"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "exits 0 and ran nothing",
        "exit_code": 1,
        "verdict": "passed",
        "kinds": [
          "no_tests"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "an exit named in the table",
        "exit_code": 1,
        "verdict": "unrunnable",
        "kinds": [
          "unrunnable"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
